From: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: do not trust prop.integrated on HIP (gfx1013 corrupts with it)

Counter-patch for the prop.integrated regression on gfx1013.

Upstream commit c7d8722 ("ggml-cuda: restore prop.integrated on HIP builds",
PR #24233) makes the HIP backend trust prop.integrated. On this board that
selects host-memory buffer paths which produce corrupted output: wikitext
perplexity reads 168.5 and 168.1 on two runs where 11.1910 is correct, at every
setting. Bisected in this repository, and confirmed by an A/B/A within one boot
that rebuilds each way and returns the correct value bit-identically when the
change is restored. An earlier revision of this header quoted the corrupted
figure as 167 from memory; it was re-measured and not left uncheckable. The non-HIP branch immediately below still carries upstream's own
comment about the same class of corruption.

That comment is the precedent for this change, not an aside. Upstream
disabled the flag for non-HIP builds because of llama.cpp issue #15034,
"Broken/no Gemma 3n output on CUDA (Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano)", which is the same
failure on the same kind of device: an integrated GPU where trusting the flag
selects host-memory buffer paths and the output comes out wrong. This patch
applies that decision to the HIP branch, where the condition was verified still
present on llama.cpp master in August 2026.

llama.cpp master has since made the same decision itself: as of 2026-09-19
ggml_cuda_init forces integrated = false on every platform, so this patch is
only needed at 7ba604f and earlier.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
---
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
         info.default_tensor_split[id] = total_vram;
         total_vram += device_vram;
 #if defined(GGML_USE_HIP)
-        info.devices[id].integrated = prop.integrated;
+        info.devices[id].integrated = false; // BC-250 test: integrated path corrupts output on gfx1013
 #else
         info.devices[id].integrated = false; // Temporarily disabled due to issues with corrupted output (e.g. #15034)
 #endif
